# Module 05: Class Members, Nested Classes, Lambdas & Enums

> **Source Track:** Oracle Java Tutorials — *Learning the Java Language*  
> **Source Lessons:** `javaOO/more.html`, `classvars.html`, `accesscontrol.html`, `initial.html`, `nested.html`, `innerclasses.html`, `localclasses.html`, `anonymousclasses.html`, `lambdaexpressions.html`, `methodreferences.html`, `whentouse.html`, `enum.html`  
> **Scope:** Static Members, Initializer Blocks, Access Modifiers, Nested/Inner/Local/Anonymous Classes, Lambdas, Method References, Enums.

---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Nested Type Taxonomy

In Java, classes can be organized hierarchically and enriched with static class-level bindings, nested internal scopes, and functional constructs.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    NC["Nested Classes"] --> SNC["Static Nested Classes<br/>(Declared static, independent of outer instance)"]
    NC --> IC["Inner Classes (Non-static)"]
    IC --> MC["Member Inner Class<br/>(Holds implicit Outer.this reference)"]
    IC --> LC["Local Class<br/>(Declared inside a method body)"]
    IC --> AC["Anonymous Class<br/>(Declared inline without a name)"]
    AC --> Lambda["Lambda Expression / Method Ref<br/>(SAM functional interface implementation via invokedynamic)"]
```

### Static Members vs. Instance Members
- **`static` Fields (Class Variables):** Exactly one memory copy exists in Metaspace/Heap, shared across all instantiated instances of the class.
- **`static` Methods:** Executed in the context of the class, not an object. **They cannot access `this` or instance variables directly**.
- **Static Initializer Blocks (`static { ... }`):** Executed exactly once when the class is loaded and initialized by the JVM classloader.
- **Instance Initializer Blocks (`{ ... }`):** Executed on every `new` instantiation *before* the constructor body runs.

---

## 2. Access Control Modifier Matrix

Java provides four levels of visibility to enforce modular encapsulation:

| Modifier | Current Class | Enclosing Package | Subclasses in Other Packages | Global / World |
| :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |
| **`public`** | Yes | Yes | Yes | Yes |
| **`protected`** | Yes | Yes | Yes (via inheritance) | No |
| **no modifier (package-private)** | Yes | Yes | No | No |
| **`private`** | Yes | No | No | No |

---

## 3. Nested Classes: Inner vs. Static Nested

### Key Distinctions
1. **Static Nested Class (`static class Helper`):**
   - Does NOT hold a reference to an instance of the outer class.
   - Behaves identically to a top-level class, merely packaged inside for namespace cohesion.
   - Cannot access non-static fields of the enclosing class directly.
2. **Inner Class (`class Helper`):**
   - Automatically maintains a hidden synthetic reference to the enclosing instance (`Outer.this`).
   - Can directly access all private fields and methods of the outer class.
   - **Hazard:** Keeping an inner class instance alive keeps the entire outer class instance alive in memory, creating subtle GC memory leaks.

---

## 4. Lambdas & Method References

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph LambdaDesugaring ["Lambda Execution Pipeline via invokedynamic"]
        Source["list.forEach(x -> System.out.println(x))"]
        Bytecode["invokedynamic opcode -> LambdaMetafactory"]
        Runtime["Generated synthetic direct call site (Zero class file overhead)"]
    end
    Source --> Bytecode --> Runtime
```

### The SAM Principle (Single Abstract Method)
A lambda expression can implement any interface that declares **exactly one abstract method** (annotated with `@FunctionalInterface`).

### Variable Capture Rules
- Lambdas can capture local variables from their enclosing lexical scope, but only if they are **`final` or effectively final** (never modified after initialization).
- Lambdas do **not** introduce a new scope for `this`. Inside a lambda, `this` refers to the enclosing class instance.

### The Four Types of Method References
1. **Reference to a static method:** `ContainingClass::staticMethodName` (e.g., `Math::max`)
2. **Reference to an instance method of a particular object:** `containingObject::instanceMethodName` (e.g., `System.out::println`)
3. **Reference to an instance method of an arbitrary object of a particular type:** `ContainingType::methodName` (e.g., `String::compareToIgnoreCase`)
4. **Reference to a constructor:** `ClassName::new` (e.g., `ArrayList::new`)

---

## 5. Enum Types: Type-Safe Enumerations

Java enums are full-featured classes extending `java.lang.Enum`.
- They provide compile-time type safety.
- Can declare private constructors, fields, instance methods, and constant-specific class bodies (abstract methods implemented per constant).
- Canonical methods: `values()` returns an array of all constants; `valueOf(String)` parses string name; `name()` returns exact declared name; `ordinal()` returns 0-based position.

---

## 6. Exhaustive Member Function & Syntax Reference

| Category | Syntax / Construct (Example) | Use Case (Code Snippet) | Specification | Description & Behavioral Invariant |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Static Initializer** | `static { ... }` | `static { DEFAULT_CONFIG = load(); }` | Once per class load | Executes during class initialization to prepare static state. |
| **Inner Class Reference**| `Outer.this.field` | `return OuterClass.this.state;` | Synthetic reference | Accesses the enclosing instance from within a non-static inner class. |
| **Lambda Syntax** | `(a, b) -> a + b` | `Comparator<Integer> c = (a, b) -> a - b;`| SAM functional | Compact syntax desugared via `LambdaMetafactory` into functional interface. |
| **Method Reference** | `Type::method` | `list.forEach(System.out::println);` | Zero-overhead delegate| Direct method handle reference avoiding explicit lambda parameter boilerplate. |
| **Enum Constants** | `Enum.values()` | `for (Role r : Role.values()) { ... }` | O(N) array copy | Returns an array containing all constants in the declared enum order. |
| **Enum ValueOf** | `Enum.valueOf("NAME")` | `Role r = Role.valueOf("ADMIN");` | O(1) hash lookup | Parses exact string matching an enum constant; throws `IllegalArgumentException` if absent. |
| **Enum Ordinal** | `e.ordinal()` | `int idx = e.ordinal();` | O(1) integer read | Returns zero-based declaration position index. |

---

## 7. Modern Idiomatic Java Code Implementation

```java
// Comprehensive demonstration of static members, lambdas, method references, and enums
package devtype.engine.advanced;

import java.util.*;
import java.util.function.BinaryOperator;

public final class AdvancedStructureLab {

    // Advanced Enum with custom fields, constructor, and constant-specific behavior
    public enum Operation {
        PLUS("+", (a, b) -> a + b),
        MINUS("-", (a, b) -> a - b),
        TIMES("*", (a, b) -> a * b),
        DIVIDE("/", (a, b) -> {
            if (b == 0) throw new ArithmeticException("Division by zero");
            return a / b;
        });

        private final String symbol;
        private final BinaryOperator<Double> action;

        Operation(String symbol, BinaryOperator<Double> action) {
            this.symbol = symbol;
            this.action = action;
        }

        public double apply(double x, double y) {
            return action.apply(x, y);
        }

        public String getSymbol() { return symbol; }
    }

    // Static nested class acting as a builder
    public static class Task {
        private final String title;
        private final Operation operation;

        private Task(Builder builder) {
            this.title = builder.title;
            this.operation = builder.operation;
        }

        public static class Builder {
            private String title = "Default";
            private Operation operation = Operation.PLUS;

            public Builder withTitle(String title) {
                this.title = title;
                return this;
            }

            public Builder withOperation(Operation op) {
                this.operation = op;
                return this;
            }

            public Task build() {
                return new Task(this);
            }
        }
    }

    // Demonstration of method references
    public static List<String> processTitles(List<String> rawTitles) {
        return rawTitles.stream()
                .filter(Objects::nonNull)           // Static method reference
                .map(String::trim)                  // Arbitrary object instance method reference
                .sorted(String::compareToIgnoreCase)// Two-argument comparator reference
                .toList();
    }
}
```

---

## 8. Common Traps, Anti-Patterns & Best Practices

1. **Outer Class Memory Leaks via Non-Static Inner Classes:**
   - *Trap:* Exporting instances of a non-static inner class across asynchronous boundaries retains the entire outer class instance in memory, preventing GC.
   - *Remedy:* Make nested classes `static` unless access to the outer instance state is strictly required.

2. **Using `enum.ordinal()` for Database Persistence or Wire Serialization:**
   - *Trap:* Persisting `ordinal()` integers causes database corruption when enum constants are reordered or new constants are inserted.
   - *Remedy:* Always persist enum `name()` strings or an explicit code attribute stored in an internal field.

3. **Mutating Variables Captured by Lambdas:**
   - *Trap:* Attempting to mutate an external counter variable (`int count = 0; list.forEach(x -> count++);`) fails compilation with *"local variables referenced from a lambda expression must be final or effectively final"*.
   - *Remedy:* Use specialized atomic wrappers (`AtomicInteger`) or reduction operations (`stream.count()`).

