# Module 16: Advanced NIO.2 — Directory Tree Walking, PathMatcher & WatchService

> **Source Track:** Oracle Java Tutorials — *Essential Java Classes*  
> **Source Lessons:** `io/walk.html`, `find.html`, `notification.html`, `misc.html`  
> **Scope:** Recursive File Tree Walking (`Files.walkFileTree`), `SimpleFileVisitor`, `FileVisitResult`, `PathMatcher` Pattern Matching (Glob vs Regex), `WatchService` Kernel Event Notifications.

---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Tree Traversal

NIO.2 provides specialized tools for deep filesystem operations:
1. **`SimpleFileVisitor<Path>`:** Depth-first recursive filesystem tree walking.
2. **`PathMatcher`:** Flexible pattern matching on filenames using **Glob syntax** (`*.{java,class}`) or Regular Expressions.
3. **`WatchService`:** Native OS-level filesystem event monitoring (Linux `inotify`, macOS `FSEvents`, Windows `ReadDirectoryChangesW`).

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    Walk["Files.walkFileTree(startPath, visitor)"]
    Walk --> Pre["preVisitDirectory(dir, attrs)"]
    Pre --> Visit["visitFile(file, attrs)"]
    Visit --> Post["postVisitDirectory(dir, ex)"]
```

---

## 2. Exhaustive Member Function & Tree Reference

| Category | Method / Syntax (Example) | Use Case (Code Snippet) | Complexity | Description & Behavioral Invariant |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Walk File Tree** | `Files.walkFileTree(p, v)`| `Files.walkFileTree(root, new CleanVisitor());` | $O(Files)$ traversal | Depth-first directory traversal visiting every file and directory. |
| **PathMatcher** | `fs.getPathMatcher("glob:*.java")`| `PathMatcher m = FileSystems.getDefault().getPathMatcher("glob:**.java");`| $O(1)$ compile | Creates pattern matcher for filenames using glob syntax. |
| **WatchService** | `path.register(ws, events)`| `path.register(watchService, StandardWatchEventKinds.ENTRY_CREATE);`| Native OS watch | Registers directory for native filesystem change notifications. |

---

## 3. Modern Idiomatic Java Code Implementation

```java
// Comprehensive demonstration of SimpleFileVisitor tree walking and directory size calculation
package devtype.engine.io;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.nio.file.*;
import java.nio.file.attribute.BasicFileAttributes;

public final class AdvancedNioLab {

    public static long calculateDirectorySize(Path rootDir) throws IOException {
        final long[] totalBytes = {0};

        Files.walkFileTree(rootDir, new SimpleFileVisitor<Path>() {
            @Override
            public FileVisitResult visitFile(Path file, BasicFileAttributes attrs) {
                totalBytes[0] += attrs.size();
                return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE;
            }

            @Override
            public FileVisitResult visitFileFailed(Path file, IOException exc) {
                System.err.println("Cannot read file: " + file);
                return FileVisitResult.CONTINUE; // Continue walking remainder
            }
        });

        return totalBytes[0];
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Common Traps, Anti-Patterns & Best Practices

1. **Symbolic Link Circular Traversal:**
   - *Trap:* Walking a filesystem with circular symlinks while passing `FileVisitOption.FOLLOW_LINKS` triggers a `FileSystemLoopException`.
   - *Remedy:* Omit `FOLLOW_LINKS` or handle link verification inside `visitFile()`.

code:
