---

## 1. Architectural Overview & Configuration Hierarchy

External configuration allows application behavior to be customized across staging, test, and production environments without recompilation. Java establishes a clear hierarchy:
1. **Command-Line Arguments (`String[] args`):** Highest priority runtime overrides.
2. **System Properties (`-Dkey=value`):** Process-wide JVM properties.
3. **Environment Variables (`System.getenv()`):** OS shell environment settings.
4. **Properties Files (`.properties`):** Persistent configuration files on disk.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    File["config.properties on Disk"] -->|"props.load(InputStream)"| Props["Properties Map in Memory"]
    Props -->|"getProperty('db.port', '5432')"| Value["'5432' (Fallback Default)"]
```

---

## 2. Exhaustive Member Function & Properties Reference

| Category | Method / Syntax (Example) | Use Case (Code Snippet) | Complexity | Description & Behavioral Invariant |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Load Properties** | `props.load(stream)` | `props.load(Files.newInputStream(path));` | O(Lines) parse | Parses `.properties` stream; handles escapes. |
| **Get Property** | `props.getProperty(k, def)`| `String port = props.getProperty("port", "8080");`| O(1) hash read | Reads configuration value with default fallback. |
| **Store Properties**| `props.store(out, comment)`| `props.store(out, "Application Config");`| O(N) stream write | Serializes properties map to text file with timestamp. |
| **Read Env** | `System.getenv("KEY")` | `String path = System.getenv("PATH");` | O(1) read | Reads environment variable from parent OS shell. |

---

## 3. Modern Idiomatic Java Code Implementation

```java
// Comprehensive demonstration of Properties loading and fallback hierarchy
package devtype.engine.platform;

import java.io.*;
import java.nio.file.Files;
import java.nio.file.Path;
import java.util.Properties;

public final class PropertiesConfigLab {

    public static Properties loadConfig(Path configPath) throws IOException {
        Properties defaults = new Properties();
        defaults.setProperty("server.port", "8080");
        defaults.setProperty("timeout.ms", "5000");

        Properties appProps = new Properties(defaults); // Fallback hierarchy
        if (Files.exists(configPath)) {
            try (InputStream in = Files.newInputStream(configPath)) {
                appProps.load(in);
            }
        }
        return appProps;
    }
}
```

---

## 4. Common Traps, Anti-Patterns & Best Practices

1. **Attempting to Mutate `System.getenv()`:**
   - *Trap:* `System.getenv()` returns an unmodifiable read-only map; calling `put()` throws `UnsupportedOperationException`.
   - *Remedy:* Use `System.setProperty()` for runtime configuration mutation.

